  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Transforming food systems to improve diet quality and resilience for the most vulnerable</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This programme aims to increase access to and consumption of affordable healthy diets by bottom of pyramid (BoP) consumers and their resilience to nutritional shocks through market-based solutions in 6 selected countries in sub-Saharan Africa by 2026. It seeks to do this through integrated food systems interventions organised around target nutritious food value chains in the focus countries, which are fostering sustainable change in demand, supply and the enabling environment for safe and nutritious foods.</narrative>
  </description>
